WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Part 1. You will hear an interviewer who is doing a survey asking a man some questions

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.960
about shopping. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 6.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:03.320
Good morning. I'm doing a survey of shoppers in Broadbeach. Would you have a few minutes

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:09.480
to spare to answer some questions? Oh, um, yes, I guess it would be OK.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:13.000
Thank you very much. Everybody seems so busy today.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Well, actually, I don't have loads of time, so...

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:22.800
Oh, yes, of course. It really won't take long. Could I start by taking your name, please?

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:28.800
I'm Lee. Martins with a Y. And is your family name spelt L-double-E?

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:35.800
It's L-E-I-G-H. Thank you. We don't actually publish your

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:41.720
name or details. It just makes it easier for me to identify people when I look at all the

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.519
results at the end. I see.

00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:52.000
And can I ask, how did you get into town today? Well, normally I catch the bus, but I'm on

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.559
my motorbike today because I'm going to work later.

00:01:55.559 --> 00:02:00.320
And could you tell me what you're doing this morning? I mean, the reason for your trip

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.760
into town? Well, I've just been to the hairdresser. You

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.800
see, I have a job interview at the council in a few days.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:12.279
Oh, really? Well, good luck with that. Thanks a lot. And now I'm on my way to buy

00:02:12.279 --> 00:02:17.000
a suit that I can wear to the interview. I don't actually own one at the moment.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.600
OK. Is that everything you're planning to do in town?

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:26.080
Yeah. Well, I've got to go and pick up my laptop. It broke a couple of days ago, so

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.960
I took it to the shop to get it fixed. They had to order a spare part, but apparently

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.199
it's ready for collection now. I can't wait to get it back.

00:02:34.199 --> 00:02:41.919
I'm sure. I hate it when my technology breaks down. One more thing. It's Saturday today.

00:02:41.919 --> 00:02:46.039
Is that when you like to do your shopping? Well, it's more of a question of when I'm

00:02:46.039 --> 00:02:51.279
free. If I'm free on a Monday, that's when I choose to come into town. The shops are

00:02:51.279 --> 00:03:04.440
less busy then, which I always prefer.

00:03:16.039 --> 00:03:42.039
Now listen and answer questions 7 to 10.

00:03:42.039 --> 00:03:46.880
So I'd like to ask you a few more questions to get your views about shopping in Broad

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.960
Beach, if that's OK? Sure. What would you like to know specifically?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.360
What would you say you like best about the shops here?

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:59.839
I'd probably say it's the service you get wherever you go.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:04.240
OK. And what do you think about the range of shops in Broad Beach?

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.320
Oh, you can get almost anything you want here. And what about recent changes? What do you

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:17.040
like and dislike about them? For example, there are a lot of new coffee shops now. Are

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:21.559
you enjoying them? No, there are too many of them. It's a shame

00:04:21.559 --> 00:04:24.959
as those places could be occupied by other kinds of shops.

00:04:24.959 --> 00:04:30.359
What would you like to see instead? Well, I think we have enough clothing shops,

00:04:30.359 --> 00:04:35.440
but there's only one place that sells books at the moment. It'd be nice to have a choice,

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.920
you know. Right. And have you been to the new shopping

00:04:38.959 --> 00:04:44.359
centre outside Broad Beach yet, Martin? Yes, once or twice. It's not that far from

00:04:44.359 --> 00:04:47.399
where I live. It's a very modern-looking building, isn't

00:04:47.399 --> 00:04:51.079
it? Yes, and it's lovely. The glass roof is certainly

00:04:51.079 --> 00:04:55.959
impressive, but my favourite thing is the plants they've put round the building. They're

00:04:55.959 --> 00:05:01.839
amazing and so big already. And what about the entertainment facilities?

00:05:01.839 --> 00:05:05.239
Have you used any of them yet? Like the new cinema?

00:05:05.239 --> 00:05:10.119
Nah, not yet. I can't see any advantage in having it there because the one in town is

00:05:10.119 --> 00:05:13.720
actually bigger. OK. Well, thank you so much for your time.

